# Parameters of one throw. The service solves a planar ballistic problem only: it
# knows nothing about where the tool is, the caller places the throw.
#
# target is the vector FROM THE THROWING POINT to the target, with the axes of the
# robot base (x forward, y left, z up). The caller owns the throwing pose and is
# the one that subtracts it, see '/testing/throw_pose'.
float32 m_obj
geometry_msgs/Point target
---
# valve opening time and launch angle over the horizon. The aiming azimuth is not
# answered: it is atan2(target.y, target.x) of the request, the caller already has it.
uint32 result_valve_us
float32 result_theta
bool answer
